1. DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Software" means the Delegator program, its source code, documentation,
configuration, build scripts, installers, and any part of them.

"Licensor" means confeden, the copyright holder of the Software.

"You" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
license.

"Non-Commercial Use" means use that is not primarily intended for or directed
toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation. Personal use, study,
research, teaching, evaluation, and use by non-profit organizations for their
non-profit activities are Non-Commercial Use. Use by or for a business in the
course of its operations, use in a product or service that is sold, licensed,
or monetized, and use to provide paid services are NOT Non-Commercial Use.

"AI System" means any machine-learning or statistical model, including large
language models, and any dataset, index, embedding store, corpus, or automated
pipeline that is created for the purpose of building, training, evaluating, or
augmenting such a model.

"Model Ingestion" means using the Software, in whole or in part, as input to
create or improve an AI System, including but not limited to: training,
pre-training, fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, distillation, evaluation or
benchmark corpora, dataset construction, embedding or vector-index generation,
and retrieval corpora used to generate outputs derived from the Software.

"Operating the Software" means running the Software for its intended purpose,
namely delegating tasks from a coding assistant or IDE agent to language-model
backends. Operating the Software is expressly NOT Model Ingestion, even when
the operator is or uses an AI agent.

